Reason: Both queries gather the same three columns (average payment, city, state) for the three customers who have the largest number of delivered orders, but `1result.sql` is the safer choice:

• It uses the portable `ROUND()` function (supported by most SQL engines) instead of the SQLite‑specific `printf()` used in `0result.sql`.  
• All other logic—filtering only “delivered” orders, summing payments per order, counting deliveries per customer_unique_id and taking the top‑3—is correct and identical to the first query.  
Therefore `1result.sql` fulfils the requirement without relying on engine‑specific syntax, making it the preferable answer.